o you know some of the corner stores  but they're being inundated with people  it's a bit of a food desert yeah a food  desert losing out you know fellow  neighbors here and then losing  what over 40 people with the blizzard so  it's quite a traumatizing few months  yeah it has been because I had like 10  people in my house and two rooms for my  store was electric so I had to use  propane to heat my house  uh I had my kids in there and  I just had to make sure that they had  heat you know because I got a 11 month  old grandbaby there many people were  surprised by the ferocity of this storm  some unprepared but there's no escaping  that certain people in this city bore  the brunt of its brutality Martha  Kellner Sky News Buffalo
 

